  "_comment": "EXPERIMENTAL 60-company CANDIDATE population for the Laya selector prototype (docs/scopes/LAYA_SELECTOR_V1.md). It is NOT used directly by any run: laya_preflight.py --freeze qualifies it for one window and writes a frozen coverage-qualified pool (watchlist/experimental_pools/), and only that pool can drive an experimental run. Separate from watchlist/watchlist.json (baseline fixed-10) and watchlist/experimental_fixed30.json (unchanged). A fixed-universe prototype: chosen with present-day knowledge, so it is survivorship-biased and says nothing about historical market-wide representativeness. Changing any entry changes universe_hash and needs a new version.",
  "_selection_method": "Recorded 2026-10-03 before any coverage check, scoring, or run. Keep all 30 fixed30-v1 names unchanged (10 baseline + 20 added), then add exactly 3 per sector bucket (6 per sector). Additions were picked by hand for liquidity, sector spread and plausible news/price provider coverage from long-listed US common stocks. Excluded a priori: biotech, recent IPOs, tickers that are ordinary English words (e.g. DOW, MOS, KEYS, HAL), and names with a known pending take-private, breakup or merger as of the selector's knowledge (e.g. EA, KHC, KDP, IPG). A read-only factual check (yfinance via maverick-mcp, 2026-10-03) confirmed each addition is a listed EQUITY on NYSE/Nasdaq with the stated sector, >= 5 years of daily bars and >= 2.2M average daily volume. No returns, momentum, backtest outcome, Laya score or future information was used. Several additions exceed the baseline RULES.md section 8 mid-cap/volume bands; the 60 are not section-8 screened.",
